---
title: Soft Bread Rolls
cooklang: 2
servings: 12
makes: 12 rolls
unit system: metric
time:
  prep: 25 minutes
  rest: 1 hour 30 minutes
  cook: 18 minutes
techniques: [knead, prove, bake]
tags: [bread, baking, beginner]
---

`Warm 37 °C` @whole milk{300%ml}|@oat milk{}?dairy-free in a #small saucepan{} until ~{just warm to the touch}, about 37 °C.

`Mix` @strong white flour{500%g}, @caster sugar{1%tbsp} and @fine salt{10%g} in a
#large bowl{}.

?yeast=fresh: `Dissolve` @fresh yeast{21%g} by crumbling it into the warm milk and
stirring until ~{smooth}.

?yeast=active-dry: `Activate` @active dry yeast{9%g} in the warm milk with a pinch of
the sugar. Leave ~{10%minutes} until ~{foamy}.

?yeast=instant: `Stir` @instant yeast{7%g} straight into the flour.

`Combine` the milk with the flour, then add @unsalted butter{40%g}(soft)|@olive oil{3%tbsp}?dairy-free.

?kneading=by-hand: `Knead` on a lightly floured surface for ~{10%minutes} until ~{smooth and springy}.

?kneading=stand-mixer: `Knead` with the dough hook of a #stand mixer{} on medium speed for
~{6%minutes}.

`Prove covered` covered in the #&large bowl{} for ~prove{1%hour} until ~{doubled}. -> dough

`Shape` the @&dough{} into 12 balls, set them on a #baking tray{} lined with
#parchment{}, and prove again for ~prove{30%minutes}.

`Bake 200 °C` at 200 °C for ~oven{15-18%minutes} until ~{golden and hollow-sounding underneath}.
